fanout.js

A fanout messaging server for node.js
by @jazzychad - Chad Etzel

+ some modifications to be the default
  messaging system for SparkleShare

MIT Licensed

Usage: subscribe <channel>
       unsubscribe <channel>
       announce <channel> <message>
       ping


This was a git submodule of github.com/nextsux/fanout.node.js, which has had no
commit since 2011 and stopped working on supported node versions (it built its
emitter from process.EventEmitter, removed from node long ago). It is vendored
here so it can be maintained, keeping the original MIT licence and attribution.

The protocol has NO AUTHENTICATION: any client that can reach the port may
subscribe to any channel and announce on any channel, so notifications are
readable and forgeable by anyone who can connect. Set config.fanout.host to an
interface only trusted clients can reach.
